              "reviewGroupId": "goal-4aa3a130-b517-5ac5-87b2-147fe432cadd-required-by-ba621c67-b750-5e45-ab37-a51ea45e3ccf",
              "physicalDecision": "approve",
              "rationale": "Photometry requires judging blank, calibration range, nonlinearity, reference-control bias and the distinction between repeatability and accuracy. Claim-specific adequacy, confounds and bounded data conclusions are necessary to deciding whether a computed concentration may be released."
            }
          ],
          "sourceDecision": "not_accepted_due_to_physical_rejection",
          "concreteJurisdictionReason": "Full selected route fails scientifically necessary prerequisite closure. Blocking physical edge group(s): 44. The data-validity tasks can judge supplied controls, cross-reactivity and temperature confounding without producing their own trend diagram or relating measured trends to an initial investigation hypothesis. Those representation/hypothesis operations make the whole prerequisite broader than necessary. Known supplied restrictions remain unresolved: Whole selected path does not pass every current prerequisite target course filter; source/course and alternative path review required.",
