              "physicalDecision": "approve",
              "rationale": "The secondary-cell tasks explain forced charging versus voluntary discharging, reconstruct reactions and assess energy for a real purpose under bounded conditions. Understanding reversible operation, distinct energy directions and why a device-empty or nonrechargeable battery is not automatically rechargeable is necessary to that stated secondary-cell function and use boundary."
            }
          ],
          "sourceDecision": "hold_source_or_scope",
          "concreteJurisdictionReason": "Original BB/BE p.53 identifies types of electrochemical sources with predominantly phenomenological GK treatment. This does not by itself require the complete reversible-cell/everyday empty-battery boundaries and detailed source-critical secondary-cell task. A more specific original source operation and exact course scope are needed.",
